@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@* The sign-in page deliberately drops the app chrome — no nav, no header — because there is
   nothing to navigate to until you are signed in.

   It still needs a <main> landmark. This layout was previously bare `@Body`, so /login was the one
   route in the app with no landmark at all: a screen-reader user landing on the page that every
   unauthenticated visit redirects to had no way to skip to content. AccessibilityUiTests asserts a
   single main landmark per route, but its theory only enumerated the five authenticated routes, so
   nothing failed. *@
<main id="main-content" class="login-main">
    @Body
</main>
